<section class="section-content bg-sec-blue" id="pre-existing-disease">
    <div class="il-container">
        <div class="cont-img-block flex-div">
            <div class="cont-block width-50">
                <h2 class="heading2">What is Pre-existing Disease in Health Insurance? </h2>
                <p class="text mt-20"> A pre-existing disease is any medical condition, illness or injury that you were diagnosed with or received treatment for within 36 months prior to your policy start date. Some common examples include asthma, diabetes, hypertension and heart conditions. Here are a few important things to know about pre-existing diseases in health insurance: </p>
                <ul class="bullet-list mt-20">
                    <li><p><strong>Always declare your PEDs: </strong>Non-disclosure can lead to claim rejection or policy cancellation. Declare everything upfront — your waiting period handles the rest, not a claim denial. </p></li>
                    <li><p><strong>Standard waiting period:</strong> Most health insurance policies have a 2–3 year waiting period for PED. Coverage for those conditions kicks in only after that period is complete. </p></li>
                    <li><p><strong>Once the waiting period is done:</strong> All pre-existing conditions are covered fully under your health insurance policy with no additional premium, no exclusions. </p></li>

                </ul>
                <p>Want to reduce that wait? With ICICI Lombard’s Jumpstart add-on (available on Elevate), your PED waiting period drops to just 30 days after policy inception. </p>

            </div>
             <div class="img-block">
                <img src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/health-revamp/pre-existing.webp" alt="Pre-existing Disease in Health Insurance" title="Pre-existing Disease in Health Insurance" class="img-hide">
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section-content" id="mediclaim-health-diff">
    <div class="il-container">
        <h2 class="heading2 align-center">What is the Difference Between Mediclaim<br> and Health Insurance? </h2>
        <p class="sub-txt mid-width align-center">The terms ‘<a href="https://www.icicilombard.com/health-insurance/mediclaim" class="link">mediclaim</a>’ and ‘health insurance’ are often used interchangeably and generally refer to the same type of financial support during hospitalisation, as per policy terms. Both help you manage eligible medical expenses during a hospital stay and support you from admission paperwork to claim submission during an emergency.  </p>
       <!-- 
<p class="text align-center mt-15 mb-20"><strong>Here’s a quick snapshot of mediclaim vs health insurance: </strong></p>
-->
