</section>


<section class="section-content bg-warmgray" id="eligibility-criteria">
    <div class="il-container">
        <h2 class="heading2 align-center">What are the Eligibility Criteria to Buy<br> Health insurance in India?</h2>
        <p class="sub-txt mid-width align-center">Your health insurance eligibility depends on multiple factors related to your health and risk profile. Some of these include your age, pre-existing diseases, lifestyle, etc. Our health insurance policies have the following eligibility criteria:</p>
       
        <div class="table-wrapper table-style1 table-style2 width-80 mt-30">
            <table class="table-wrap">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th style="width: 30%">Eligibility Criteria</th>
                        <th style="width: 70%">Specifications</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td class="strong-txt" style="width: 30%">Age - Adults</td>
                        <td style="width: 70%">Adults aged 18 years and up to 125 years</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td class="strong-txt">Age - Children</td>
                        <td>Child aged 6 years and above (proposer must be above 18 years) can be covered under an individual health policy.<br>
Dependent children aged 91 days to 30 years can be covered under a family floater health insurance.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td class="strong-txt">Nationality</td>
                        <td>Indian residents and NRIs</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                       <td class="strong-txt">Policy Type</td>
                        <td>Individual and family floater</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                       <td class="strong-txt">Waiting Period</td>
                        <td>Initial waiting period of 30 days; Specified Disease waiting period of 2 years; and Pre-existing disease waiting period of 3 years</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <div class="width-80">
            <ul class="bullet-list mt-20">
                <li><p class="text">Age criteria: Anyone aged 18 years and above can buy health insurance online. You can also add your spouse, dependent children (aged 91 days to 30 years) and parents to your policy.</p></li>
                <li><p class="text">Nationality: You need to be an Indian citizen to secure yourself with a medical insurance in India. Many insurers are now also offering health insurance coverage to NRIs.</p></li>
                <li><p class="text">Pre-existing Diseases: Having an existing health condition can influence your health insurance policy eligibility. You need to serve a waiting period before getting coverage for them.</p></li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

