<section class="section-content bg-pink" id="calculate-health-premium">
    <div class="il-container">
        <div class="cont-list-block flex-div">
            <div class="cont-block left-block">
                <h2 class="heading2">How to Calculate Health Insurance Premiums?</h2>
                <p class="text">Your health insurance premium is calculated based on factors like your age, type of coverage, sum insured and add-ons selected, location, applicable discounts, etc. Knowing how premiums are calculated can help you plan better and choose a health insurance policy that fits both your budget and medical needs. Here’s a quick dive into different factors needed to calculate your health insurance premium online:</p>
            </div>
            <div class="list-block org-list right-block">
                <ul>
                    <li class="text"><strong>Age:</strong> It plays a huge role in determining your premium. The lower the age, the lower the amount you need to pay as insurers generally consider young individuals less likely to need frequent medical care.</li>
                    <li class="text"><strong>Number of People Covered:</strong> Your health insurance premium also depends on whether you want to insure just yourself or your loved ones as well. Insuring multiple members can increase your overall health insurance premium amount.</li>
                    <li class="text"><strong>Type of Coverage:</strong> This is another factor that affects your premium. Different policy types, like individual health insurance, family floater health insurance, mediclaim policy or critical illness insurance, have different coverage scope and premium structures.</li>
                    <li class="text"><strong>Coverage Amount:</strong> Your premium is directly linked to the sum insured you choose. A health insurance policy with a higher sum insured will help to cover higher medical expenses but also increase the premium amount.</li>
                    <li class="text"><strong>Add-ons:</strong> Opting for optional covers like Jumpstart, OPD+ Rider, Worldwide Cover, Infinite Care, etc helps to enhance your coverage and provides well-round protection. But these add-ons also increase your premium amount.</li>
                    <li class="text"><strong>Location:</strong> Medical costs vary across cities and zones, and insurance companies factor this in while calculating premiums. As a result, premiums may be higher in metro cities compared to smaller towns.</li>
                </ul>

                <p class="text mt-20">You can also use a health insurance calculator to get a fair idea about your payable medical insurance premium.</p>

                <a href="/health-insurance/health-insurance-premium-calculator" class="primary-btn buy-now-btn calc-prem-btn full-btn-width" target="_blank">Calculate Premium Now</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

