<section class="section-content owl-div bg-warmgray" id="reduce-health-prem">
    <div class="il-container">
        <h2 class="heading2 align-center">How to Reduce Your Health Insurance Premiums?</h2>
        <p class="sub-txt align-center">While it is important to understand which factors affect your medical insurance premium, you can consider the following tips to reduce it:</p>
        <div class="row-block reduce-health-block owl-sec owl-carousel owl-theme mt-20">
            <div class="row-item bg-white">
                <div class="img-wrap"><img src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/health-revamp/compare-policy.webp" alt="Health Premium - Compare Policies Online" title="Health Premium - Compare Policies Online"></div>
                <div class="row-cont">
                    <h3 class="heading3">Compare Policies Online</h3>
                    <p class="text mt-10">Not all health plans are the same. You may end up compromising on your coverage by choosing the cheapest health insurance. So, thoroughly compare health insurance policies online to find the one that best suits your budget and coverage needs. </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row-item bg-white">
                <div class="img-wrap"><img src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/health-revamp/choose-right-sum.webp" alt="Health Premium - Choose Right Sum Insured" title="Health Premium - Choose Right Sum Insured"></div>
                <div class="row-cont">
                    <h3 class="heading3">Choose the Right Sum Insured</h3>
                    <p class="text mt-10">Select a sum insured that adequately meets your healthcare requirements without emptying your pocket. It is important to find the right balance between sufficient health insurance coverage and a premium you find affordable.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row-item bg-white">
                <div class="img-wrap"><img src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/health-revamp/buy-health-insure.webp" alt="Health Premium - Buy Health Insurance Early" title="Health Premium - Buy Health Insurance Early"></div>
                <div class="row-cont">
                    <h3 class="heading3">Buy Health Insurance Early</h3>
                    <p class="text mt-10">Young people are usually healthier than their older counterparts. Hence, they enjoy lower premiums. Buying the best health insurance in your 20s and 30s helps you to get lower rates and avoid higher premiums later.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row-item bg-white">
                <div class="img-wrap"><img src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/health-revamp/select-long-tenure.webp" alt="Health Premium - Select Long-Tenure Coverage" title="Health Premium - Select Long-Tenure Coverage"></div>
                <div class="row-cont">
                    <h3 class="heading3">Select Long-Tenure Coverage</h3>
                    <p class="text mt-10">Choosing a long-term health insurance policy helps you to lock in coverage for multiple years. This helps you to avoid yearly renewals and coverage gaps. It also attracts amazing discounts from the insurer.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row-item bg-white">
                <div class="img-wrap"><img src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/health-revamp/voluntary-copay.webp" alt="Health Premium - Opt for Voluntary Co-Payment/Deductible" title="Health Premium - Opt for Voluntary Co-Payment/Deductible"></div>
                <div class="row-cont">
                    <h3 class="heading3">Opt for Voluntary Co-Payment/Deductible</h3>
                    <p class="text mt-10">You can get discounts on health insurance premiums by opting for voluntary co-payment or deductible. These two are useful options to reduce your premium whilst keeping your coverage intact. </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row-item bg-white">
                <div class="img-wrap"><img src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/health-revamp/healthy-lifestyle.webp" alt="Health Premium - Follow Healthy Lifestyle" title="Health Premium - Follow Healthy Lifestyle"></div>
                <div class="row-cont">
                    <h3 class="heading3">Follow a Healthy Lifestyle</h3>
                    <p class="text mt-10">Health insurance companies usually reward their customers for maintaining a healthy lifestyle. You can participate in wellness programmes and preventive health check-ups to earn reward points, which can be redeemed to avail discount on premiums. </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row-item bg-white">
                <div class="img-wrap"><img src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/health-revamp/looking-discount.webp" alt="Health Premium - Look for Discounts" title="Health Premium - Look for Discounts"></div>
                <div class="row-cont">
                    <h3 class="heading3">Look for Discounts</h3>
                    <p class="text mt-10">Many insurers offer multiple discounts to attract policyholders. For example, ICICI Lombard offers discount for buying health insurance policy online, having a good credit score, opting a voluntary deductible, etc.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section-content owl-div" id="common-mistake">
    <div class="il-container">
        <h2 class="heading2 align-center">What are the Common Mistakes Made While<br> Buying Health Insurance?</h2>
        <div class="flex-div mt-40 read-more-list">
            <div class="list-block org-list width-equal org-list-block">
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <h4 class="heading4">Focusing Only on Premium</h4>
                        <p class="text">This is one of the most common mistakes people do while buying insurance policy. Remember, the best health insurance policy for you is the one that provides comprehensive coverage at a reasonable price.</p>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <h4 class="heading4">Not Comparing Policies Online</h4>
                        <p class="text">Never buy a health insurance policy without comparing multiple options available in the market. Different policies have different benefits, coverages and exclusions. Compare health insurance policies online and choose the one that meet all your healthcare requirements.</p>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <h4 class="heading4">Choosing Insufficient Sum Insured</h4>
                        <p class="text">Some people underestimate future medical costs while others opt for a lower sum insured to save on premium. Always choose a sum insured by taking your healthcare and lifestyle needs into consideration.</p>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <h4 class="heading4">Buying Health Insurance Too Late</h4>
                        <p class="text">Don’t wait for a medical emergency to realise the need for health insurance. Delaying the purchase can result in higher premiums or longer waiting periods. Buying early helps you to save on premiums and complete waiting periods sooner. </p>
                    </li>
            </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="list-block org-list width-equal org-list-block">
                <ul>
                    <li class="more-list-show">
                        <h4 class="heading4">Not Declaring Pre-existing Diseases</h4>
                        <p class="text">Keeping your pre-existing health condition a secret can lead to claim rejection or policy cancellation later. You should always disclose your pre-existing diseases, be it asthma or diabetes, at the time of policy purchase.</p>
                    </li>

                    <li class="more-list-show">
                        <h4 class="heading4">Overlooking Waiting Periods</h4>
                        <p class="text">Many people don’t check the waiting periods applicable in their health insurance policies. Always review the waiting period for pre-existing diseases, maternity coverage or specific treatments to avoid surprises during claims.</p>
                    </li>

                     <li class="more-list-show">
                        <h4 class="heading4">Ignoring Co-payments/Sub-limits</h4>
                        <p class="text">While purchasing a medical insurance, many people overlook room rent limits, co-payment clauses and treatment-specific sub-limits. Ignoring these can significantly increase your out-of-pocket expenses during claims.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <a href="javascript:;" class="read-more-link">Read more</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section-content bg-sec-blue" id="IRDAI-health">
    <div class="il-container">
        <div class="mid-width">
                <h2 class="heading2 align-center">What is the Role of IRDAI in Health Insurance?</h2>
                <div class="list-block org-list org-list-block mt-20">
                    <ul>
                        <li>
                            <h4 class="heading4">Policy Regulation</h4>
                            <p class="text">It regulates how health insurance policies are designed, priced and offered. It controls policy terms, benefits, exclusions and premium structures.</p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <h4 class="heading4">Licencing</h4>
                            <p class="text">The IRDAI has the authority to grant, renew, modify, suspend or cancel the licence of insurance companies and intermediaries.</p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <h4 class="heading4">Policyholder Protection</h4>
                            <p class="text">It protects customer in matters related to policy terms and conditions, nominations, claim settlement, surrender value, etc.</p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <h4 class="heading4">Grievance Redressal</h4>
                            <p class="text">The IRDAI has a formal escalation mechanism to help policyholders. You can escalate unresolved complaints through its grievance redressal systems.</p>
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section-content" id="myths-health">
    <div class="il-container">
        <h2 class="heading2 align-center">What are the Common Health Insurance Myths in India?</h2>

        <div class="grad-box owl-carousel owl-theme">
            <div class="grad-box-item">
                <h3 class="heading3">Myth 1</h3>
                <p class="text strong-txt">Young and healthy people don’t need health insurance </p>
                <p class="text mt-10">Most people think health insurance is only for old and sick people. However, recent data shows that feeling healthy doesn’t always mean your body truly is healthy since lifestyle-related conditions develop silently without showing any major symptoms. Hence, it is important to buy health insurance early and complete waiting periods before hidden conditions become serious. </p>
            </div>
            <div class="grad-box-item">
                <h3 class="heading3">Myth 2</h3>
                <p class="text strong-txt">Corporate health insurance is enough </p>
                <p class="text mt-10">Many corporate employees depend on the group health insurance offered by their employer. While it offers basic protection for hospitalisation and listed medical procedures, the coverage is usually limited and non-customisable. Having a separate health insurance policy ensures you continue to stay covered even if you change or leave your job. </p>
            </div>
            <div class="grad-box-item">
                <h3 class="heading3">Myth 3</h3>
                <p class="text strong-txt">I don’t need to declare pre-existing diseases</p>
                <p class="text mt-10">It is essential to declare any pre-existing health conditions to avoid policy cancellation or claim rejection in the future. All you need to do is disclose your medical history at the time of buying health insurance and serve the applicable waiting period. However, under our Elevate policy, you can get coverage for pre-existing diseases from day 31 by opting for JumpstartAG add-on.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="grad-box-item">
                <h3 class="heading3">Myth 4</h3>
                <p class="text strong-txt">Health insurance is useful only during hospitalisation</p>
                <p class="text mt-10">Today, most health insurance policies extend benefits beyond hospital stays. They also cover pre and post hospitalisation expenses, day care treatment, ambulance expenses, teleconsultations, OPD expenses, health check-ups and more. ICICI Lombard also rewards healthy behaviour, making health insurance useful even when you are not hospitalised.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="grad-box-item">
                <h3 class="heading3">Myth 5</h3>
                <p class="text strong-txt">Health insurance covers everything</p>
                <p class="text mt-10">Even the best health insurance policies come with certain inclusions, exclusions, waiting periods, and other terms and conditions. For example, they may not cover certain <a href="/docs/default-source/other-documents/sc-annexure---non-payable-list.pdf?sfvrsn=2" class="link" target="_blank">non-medical and non-payable expenses</a>. That’s why you should thoroughly read the policy wordings/documents to understand what is covered and avoid claim-time surprises.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section-content owl-div bg-amber" id="make-claim">
    <div class="il-container">
        <h2 class="heading2 align-center">How to Make a Claim for Your Health Insurance?</h2>
        <p class="text align-center mid-width">You can easily file a health insurance claim with ICICI Lombard. Choose a cashless claim if you get treated at a network hospital or opt for a reimbursement claim if you receive treatment at a non-network hospital. </p>
        <div class="first-sec-fold owl-fold owl-carousel owl-theme">
            <div class="fold-box first-fold">
                <h3 class="heading3">Cashless Claim</h3>
                <div class="series-block">
                    <div class="series-item">
                        <div class="series-no">1</div>
                        <p class="series-txt">Visit the nearest network hospital.  </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="series-item">
                        <div class="series-no">2</div>
                        <p class="series-txt">The hospital needs to send your pre-authorisation request up to 48 hours before a planned hospitalisation or within 24 hours of emergency hospitalisation.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="series-item">
                        <div class="series-no">3</div>
                        <p class="series-txt">We will process your cashless hospitalisation request as per the policy terms and conditions.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="series-item">
                        <div class="series-no">4</div>
                        <p class="series-txt">You can go ahead with the treatment once the hospital receives approval from our end.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="series-item">
                        <div class="series-no">5</div>
                        <p class="series-txt">After your treatment is done, we will directly settle your admissible hospitalisation bill. You can track your claim status on the IL TakeCare App.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="fold-box second-fold">
                <h3 class="heading3">Reimbursement Claim</h3>
                <div class="series-block">
                    <div class="series-item">
                        <div class="series-no">1</div>
                        <p class="series-txt">Get medical treatment at any hospital of your choice and pay the bills upfront.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="series-item">
                        <div class="series-no">2</div>
                        <p class="series-txt">You can raise a health insurance reimbursement claim via our website or IL TakeCare App.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="series-item">
                        <div class="series-no">3</div>
                        <p class="series-txt">Submit a duly filled claim form along with self-attested supporting documents (in PDF/ JPEG format) on the app or website.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="series-item">
                        <div class="series-no">4</div>
                        <p class="series-txt">You can also send these documents to the following address: ICICI Lombard General Insurance Co. Ltd, Varun Towers-II, 1st, 4th (Half), 5th and 6th floors, Opp. Hyderabad Public School, Begum pet, Hyderabad, Telangana 500016.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="series-item">
                        <div class="series-no">5</div>
                        <p class="series-txt">We’ll reimburse the admissible claim amount to your bank account.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <p class="text align-center mt-30">For detailed information about <a href="/health-insurance/health-claim" class="link" target="_blank">ICICI Lombard’s claim process.</a></p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Sahayak start -->

