</div><div class='sfContentBlock'><section class="section-content bg-coolgray tab-accord-sec" id="faq-sec">
    <div class="il-container">
        <h2 class="heading2 align-center">Frequently Asked Questions on Health Insurance</h2>

        <div class="tab-sec">
            <ul>
                <li class="active" id="general"><span>General</span></li>
                <li id="coverage"><span>Coverage</span></li>
                <li id="premium" class=""><span>Premium</span></li>
                <li id="claims" class=""><span>Claims</span></li>
                <li id="renewal" class=""><span>Renewal</span></li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="accord-wrap">
            <div class="accordian-block accord-sec" data-rel="general">
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">What is sum insured in health insurance?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Sum insured is the maximum amount that an insurance company will pay in the event of a claim in a policy year. Suppose you have an annual sum insured of ₹10 lakhs and your hospitalisation bill amounts to ₹12 lakhs. In this case, your insurer will pay up to ₹10 lakhs as per the policy’s terms and conditions.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">What do you mean by a pre-existing disease?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">A pre-existing disease refers to any health condition or illness diagnosed about 36 months prior to buying a health insurance policy. You need to complete the applicable waiting period before your policy starts covering the disclosed pre-existing disease.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                  <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">What do you mean by waiting period?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Waiting period is the specified period of time you need to wait before you can enjoy coverage for certain illnesses, treatments or pre-existing diseases.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">If I increase my sum insured at the time of renewal, does a waiting period apply?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes. The increased sum insured will attract a waiting period.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                  <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">My employer provides me with a health insurance. Do I still need one?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes. While having a corporate health insurance is helpful, the coverage ends when you switch jobs. Therefore, it is important to insure yourself with a comprehensive health insurance to ensure continuous, customisable coverage.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">From what age can I include my children in the plan?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">You can include your children aged 90 days to 30 years in your family floater health insurance policy.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Which is the best health insurance policy for me?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">It depends on your needs. For example, you can opt for a family floater health insurance if you want to cover multiple family members under a single policy. However, you can also opt for an individual health insurance policy for wider coverage.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">What is the advantage of buying health insurance?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Health insurance not only protects you from rising medical costs but also provides cashless hospitalisation, day care treatments, wellness programmes, health check-ups, etc. Apart from this, you can also get tax benefits on your health insurance policy under the old tax regime.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Can a person have more than one health insurance policy?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes. You can buy multiple health insurance policies to cover your medical costs. If one insurer rejects your claim, there is still a chance that others may accept as per their terms and conditions.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">How does lifestyle (smoking/alcohol consumption) affect health insurance premium?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Smoking or drinking regularly may increase the chances of health issues in the future and health insurance companies factor it into their underwriting and pricing structure.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">What is the right age to buy a health insurance policy?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Health insurance premiums are generally lower when you are young and healthy. This helps you save money. Additionally, buying early helps you complete waiting periods for specific illnesses before you might actually need them.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">What is the difference between sum insured and sum assured?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Sum insured is the maximum amount you can get when you file a health insurance claim whereas sum assured is the fixed payout paid under a life insurance policy on death or maturity.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="accordian-block accord-sec" data-rel="coverage">
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Is health insurance mandatory in India?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">No, but it is strongly recommended as health insurance policy protects you against rising healthcare costs.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Can NRIs or foreigners living in India buy health insurance?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes, NRIs can buy medical insurance for themselves and their families (spouse, children and parents) residing in India, subject to underwriting norms.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Can minors buy health insurance independently?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">No. Minors cannot buy a health insurance policy independently. However, parents can serve as proposers for stand-alone child policies for children greater than 6 years. Also,&nbsp; parents can cover their children aged 90 days to 30 years under their family floater health insurance.  </p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Does health insurance cover OPD expenses?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes, OPD expenses are covered only if you have opted for the OPD+ rider or BeFit add-on with your ICICI Lombard health insurance policy.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Is health insurance valid outside India?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Most health insurance policies offer usually domestic coverage. However, you can opt for Worldwide Cover add-on to get international coverage.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Can I change the nominee during the policy term?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes. You can change or update your nominee by submitting an endorsement request via your insurer’s website or mobile app.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Are daycare procedures covered under health insurance?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes. Day care procedures/treatment are one of the basic covers offered by ICICI Lombard health insurance policies.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Does health insurance cover modern treatments like robotic surgery?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes. Elevate health insurance covers robotic surgeries under its Technological Advancements and Treatments cover.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Are diagnostic tests like MRI, CT scan and PET scan covered?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes, health insurance policies cover diagnostic tests when they are part of hospitalisation and medically necessary.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Is home treatment or domiciliary hospitalisation covered?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes, if treatment is taken at home due to medical necessity and subject to policy conditions.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Are alternative treatments like AYUSH covered?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes, ICICI Lombard health insurance covers AYUSH treatments.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Does health insurance cover maternity expenses?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">You can get coverage for maternity expenses by opting the Maternity Benefit (add-on) available under our Elevate health insurance. </p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Are ambulance charges covered in health insurance?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes. ICICI Lombard health insurance covers road ambulance expenses.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Which diseases are permanently excluded from health insurance?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Depends on your health insurance policy. You can go through the exclusions listed in your policy document for detailed information. </p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                 <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">What to do if I am admitted to a non-network hospital?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">When you get treatment at a non-network hospital, you need to pay for the medical costs out of your pocket first and later raise the bills with your insurer for reimbursement. You can also check with your insurer to avail cashless treatment through the ‘Cashless Everywhere’ Initiative.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="accordian-block accord-sec" data-rel="premium">
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">How does the GST waiver affect my health insurance premium?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">With the 18% GST waiver, you now pay only the premium amount for your health insurance and no additional taxes. All this without compromising on coverage!</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                 <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Will my existing health insurance policy also receive the GST benefit?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes. All existing health policies that are due for renewal will be GST-free.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                 <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">How much GST do I have to pay on health insurance?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Effective 22nd September 2025, GST on health insurance has been reduced to 0%. This means your health insurance is GST-free.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                 <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Does premium increase every year with age?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes. Premiums typically increase with age as the risk of health issues increases over time. Also, for family floater health insurance policies, the premium is based on the age of the eldest family member.&nbsp;</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                 <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Is it cheaper to buy health insurance at a younger age?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes. Buying health insurance early helps to lock in coverage at a comparatively lower premium.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Does choosing a higher deductible reduce premium?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes, opting for a higher voluntary deductible amount can lower your health insurance premium.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Are discounts available for buying multi-year health insurance plans?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes. ICICI Lombard offers a 10% discount on 2-year policies and a 15% discount on 3-, 4-, or 5-year health insurance (Elevate).</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">How many years do we need to pay for health insurance?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">You need to pay health insurance premium for as long as you want continuous coverage and uninterrupted benefits. </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Can I buy health insurance in EMIs?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes. You can pay health insurance premium in monthly, quarterly or half-yearly instalments. </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="accordian-block accord-sec" data-rel="claims">
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">How long does health insurance claim settlement take?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">It differs from insurer to insurer. ICICI Lombard generally settles both cashless and reimbursement claims within the timelines prescribed by the IRDAI, subject to document submission.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">How to avail a cashless treatment?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">It’s simple to file a cashless claim with ICICI Lombard. Just follow these steps:</p>
                        <div class="list-block arrow-list">
                            <ul class="mt-15">
                                <li class="text mb-10">Get admitted to a network hospital</li>
                                <li class="text mb-10">Inform ICICI Lombard through the hospital’s insurance desk or our website/IL TakeCare App, and submit the pre-authorisation form. </li>
                                <li class="text mb-10">Once approved, we will settle the hospital bills as per policy terms.</li>
                                <li class="text mb-10">For detailed info, please click <a href="https://www.icicilombard.com/health-insurance/health-claim/" class="link" target="_blank">here</a>.</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">What are the documents needed to file a reimbursement claim?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">You need to submit a duly filled claims form, ID proof, bank details, discharge summary, final hospital and pharmacy bills, investigation reports, and any other documents requested by your insurer.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Can I track my health insurance claim status online?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes, you can easily track the status of your health insurance claim on our website and IL TakeCare App.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">What is the maximum number of claims allowed in a year?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">You can file multiple claims under a health insurance policy as long as they fall within the sum insured and adhere to policy terms.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="accordian-block accord-sec" data-rel="renewal">
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Can I increase my sum insured at the time of renewal?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes. You can increase your sum insured under your health insurance policy during renewal (subject to payment of additional premium for the enhanced sum insured).</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Do waiting periods reset after renewal?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">No, waiting periods do not reset as long as you renew your health insurance policy on time.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Is medical test required again at the time of renewal?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Generally, medical tests are not required at the time of policy renewal. Check with your insurer for more information.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">What happens if I miss my health insurance renewal date?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Missing your renewal date can lead to your health insurance policy lapse and loss of benefits. </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Is there a grace period for health insurance renewal?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes, ICICI Lombard offers a grace period of 30 days. You need to renew your health insurance policy during this period to retain your policy coverage and benefits. </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Can I port my health insurance policy at renewal without losing benefits?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes, you can easily port your health insurance policy without losing your accrued waiting period and benefits. </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

